	(text "U20 nRF9151 SiP -- host MCU (replaces the BT840 as host)\nPin map = nRF9151 PS v1.0 Pin assignments (HTML PS; PDF download blocked, see connectivity_notes.md).\nGPIO allocation: connectivity_notes.md section 2 is the single source of truth.\nUNUSED, left open per Nordic: SIM_DET (must float), AUX (may float), MAGPIO0-2, MIPI RFFE SDATA/SCLK/VIO,\nRESERVED 31-33 (solder only) and 81-104 (do not connect). COEX0 = GNSS LNA enable (active high, HDG COEX).\nAll 32 P0 GPIOs are used -- no spares, ETM trace pins P0.21-25 are taken as GPIO.\nFOOTPRINT IS A PLACEHOLDER: pad geometry was not readable (PS drawing is an image). Do not fab."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.42 90.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "34ade72e-2ccc-4ad3-adbc-4528800d7457")
	)
	(text "LTE antenna path (nRF9151 ANT pin 35, 50 ohm, DC grounded -- HDG ANT).\nHDG ANT: a matching network of at least three components is typically needed close to the antenna -> pi pads\nC130 (DNP) / R130 (0R) / C131 (DNP); values to be tuned on the built board. Place the pi next to J10.\nConducted test: J10 itself (u.FL to the bench), or steer to J13 by moving R130 -> R131 (HDG ANT: consider a test\nconnector; it must not deteriorate the line impedance). D101 DNP ESD (HDG ANT: additional ESD recommended).\nAUX (pin 37) unused, left open (HDG AUX: may be left floating)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 325.12 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "519d2882-54eb-45a2-badf-fd27516fa87d")
	)
	(text "Connectivity -- nRF9151 host (U20) + BT840 BLE bridge (U3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "55555555-0000-4000-8000-000000000001")
	)
	(text "C5/C6/C7: kept from the previous revision, on +3V3 at BT840 VDD (9)/VDDH (F4).\nGeneric values, not from the Fanstel datasheet (it only asks for a ripple-free\nsupply, or a ferrite + >= 47 uF at the module for noisy ones).\nR37/R38 I2C pull-ups 2.2k -> 3.3k: host is now the nRF9151, standard-drive sink\nonly 1 mA min at 0.4 V (PS GPIO IOL,SD). 3.3k = 0.88 mA; ~107 pF at 400 kHz.\nR39 FG_ALRT stays 2.2k (MAX17048 sinks it; the nRF9151 only reads it)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 396.24 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "85f1d8e5-44ad-4e44-92b8-efd3e90f49de")
	)
	(text "Local test pads (sheet-local nets only; contract nets get theirs on testpoints.kicad_sch). TP40-TP59 used here\n(no TP block was allocated to this sheet; TP1-TP21 exist, TP100+ belong to testpoints)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 353.06 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "91e2ee92-f647-4ede-8bfd-977735d7e2ca")
	)
	(text "GNSS front end (nRF9151 GPS pin 42, 50 ohm, DC grounded -- HDG GNSS). Mirrors the nRF9151 DK: LNA enabled by COEX0\n(DK UG GNSS; HDG COEX: COEX0 = external GNSS LNA control, active high, AT%XCOEX0). LNA = Infineon BGA524N6 (verified DS rev 3.5):\nC123 1 nF DC block (DS Table 6 C1, mandatory here: AI abs max 0.9 V and the bias-tee puts DC on GNSS_ANT), L101 8.2 nH\ninput match (DS Table 6 L1, Murata LQW type), C129 1 uF VCC bypass (DS Table 6 C2). PON tied to VCC (PON max = VCC+0.3 V).\nU25 TPS7A0228 2.8 V LDO, EN = COEX0: powers LNA and (via DNP R122/L100) an active antenna on J11, like the DK feeding\nan active antenna through J2. LNA bypass: fit R124, remove R123. Pi pads C124/R125/C125 at the GPS pin, C126 at J11.\nD100 DNP: HDG GNSS recommends ESD beyond the on-chip ESD (part not chosen). NO pre-filter: HDG GNSS warns a coupled\nLTE TX can damage an external LNA and recommends filter-before-LNA -- open risk, see notes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 238.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9b7cb13b-3013-455f-a63d-8aaada440737")
	)
	(text "nRF9151 VDD_GPIO (from +3V3). HDG ENABLE sequence: apply VDD_GPIO >= 6 ms after VDD and ENABLE; remove it first.\nMet on the regulation sheet: +3V3 rises 12-41 ms after +VBAT_LTE and falls first (power handoff), so R103 0R is fitted.\nDNP fallback: U21 TPS22917 + RC delay (R102 100k / C105 1 uF from NRF_VDD) -- remove R103, fit U21/R102/C105/C106/R155.\nENABLE = NRF_VDD (= +VBAT_LTE via FB10) through R101 10k + C104; the +3V3 delay assumes this. R104 = current-measure link.\nC107/C108 = HDG C6 4.7 uF / C5 100 nF at VDD_GPIO pin 65 (HDG VDD_GPIO). C109 = HDG C7 4.7 uF at DEC0 (HDG DEC0).\nC110 = HDG C8 100 nF bypass at nRESET pin 9. The HDG R2 1k series R is R313 on programming_debug (header side); no pull-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a8777a2f-770c-4450-b8b3-aa56f037df53")
	)
	(text "UICC: nano-SIM J12 (GCT SIM8060-6-0-14-00-A) and DNP eSIM/MFF2 U23, steered by 0R links (fit ONE set).\nHDG UICC: external ESD/EMI filtering recommended between card slot and nRF9151 -- TPD3F303 is one of the two parts\nNordic names. TI SLVSAM5A Fig. 6: socket on the OUT side, controller on the IN side; DATA1 = RST, DATA2 = I/O.\nC111 = 100 nF on SIM_1V8 (HDG: 100-220 nF can be considered). Test pads on SIM_RST/CLK/IO per HDG UICC.\neSIM MFF2 pad map NOT verified (placeholder footprint). The DK has an unpopulated MFF2 footprint too (DK UG)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "da6135f0-de81-4ff3-8b85-708f377562bb")
	)
	(text "nRF9151 VDD (from +VBAT_LTE)  -- values = nRF9151 HDG Schematic design BOM (C1-C4, FB1, R1)\nFB10 = HDG FB1 BLM18SD220SN1 (22R@100MHz, 6 A, 8 mOhm, 0603), placed at VDD per HDG VDD.\nC100/C101 = HDG C1/C2 1 uF (optional, place at the source side). C102/C103 = HDG C3 47 uF / C4 10 uF at the VDD pin.\nR101 = HDG R1 10k ENABLE series resistor (always-on: ENABLE tied to VDD, HDG ENABLE). C104 DNP = optional ENABLE cap.\nNordic example parts are 0201/0402; 0603/0805 used here per repo standard (HDG: keep DCR and frequency\ncharacteristics close to the selected component). Peak supply ~500 mA at 3.7 V (HDG Maximum output power)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e2b92f44-76ab-49ab-8999-bf764c519de3")
	)
	(text "nRF9151-side series links (0R default). HDG GPIOs: 100R-1k series resistors near the pin can be\nused to slow edges near the radio -- try 33-100R on UWB_SCK/MOSI if LTE/GNSS desense is seen.\nI2C: per-bus link here; per-device links belong to the sensor sheets."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 106.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e5a1fdbd-3978-4ca7-afc2-88fbb338bede")
	)
	(text "BT840 = BLE bridge. UART cross-over is done HERE; labels stay in nRF9151 terms:\n  BRIDGE_TXD (nRF9151 TX) -> R140 -> BT840 P0.26 (RX)\n  BRIDGE_RXD (nRF9151 RX) <- R141 <- BT840 P0.27 (TX)\n  BRIDGE_CTS (nRF9151 in) <- R142 <- BT840 P0.11 (RTS)\n  BRIDGE_RTS (nRF9151 out) -> R143 -> BT840 P1.00 (CTS)\n  BRIDGE_IRQ <- R144 <- BT840 P0.13.  LED_LINK = P0.02 (pin 5).  Reset = pin 14.\nCastellated pins only (probe/rework without X-ray). B4/B5/C3/D2 still avoided.\nP0.00/P0.01 free for an optional 32.768 kHz crystal; P0.09/P0.10 are NFC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 396.24 93.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ed3851e4-4727-4e2e-b268-9038a37ee6cf")
	)
